---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/astro/Footer.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - PantryPal"
  description="Privacy Policy for the PantryPal app for iPhone and Android. Learn what stays on your phone, what is sent to OpenAI, Open Food Facts and Google Firebase, and the choices you have."
  canonical="https://coachie-ai.com/privacy-policy-pantrypal"
  ogTitle="Privacy Policy - PantryPal"
  ogDescription="How the PantryPal app for iPhone and Android handles your information."
  noIndex={false}
>
  <main id="main-content" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-500 mb-8">How the PantryPal app for iPhone and Android handles your information</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">Effective date: 27 September 2026</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-10">Last updated: 27 September 2026</p>

    <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none space-y-8">

      <!-- Introduction -->
      <section>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          This Privacy Policy explains what information the PantryPal mobile app ("PantryPal", "the app") uses, where it goes, why, and the choices you have. PantryPal is built so that most of your information never leaves your phone. Please read it together with our <a href="/terms-of-use-pantrypal" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">Terms of Use</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 1. Who we are -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">1. Who we are</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          PantryPal is published by <strong>Veera</strong>, an individual developer based in India ("we", "us", "our"). We are the data controller (called the "Data Fiduciary" under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023) for the limited information described in this policy.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
          <li>Email for privacy questions and requests: <a href="mailto:contact@coachie-ai.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">contact@coachie-ai.com</a></li>
          <li>Grievance Officer (India): Veera, reachable at <a href="mailto:contact@coachie-ai.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">contact@coachie-ai.com</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. Summary -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">2. Summary</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm sm:text-base border border-gray-200">
            <thead class="bg-gray-50">
              <tr>
                <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Topic</th>
                <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">In short</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Account</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">There is no sign-up and no account. We do not ask for your name, email or phone number.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Your kitchen data</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">Your pantry, shopping list, recipes, preferences and history are stored only on your phone, in an encrypted database. We cannot see them.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Photos</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">When you choose to scan, the photo is sent to OpenAI to identify food. PantryPal never saves your photos, on the phone or anywhere else.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Recipe ideas</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">The food names in your pantry, with your diets, allergies and household size, are sent to OpenAI to create recipes.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Voice</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">Voice commands are recognised on your phone. Audio is never recorded or sent anywhere.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Analytics and crashes</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">Anonymous usage counts (which screens are used, how many items a scan found) and crash reports go to Google Firebase. Never your food names or anything you type. You can turn analytics off in Settings.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Payments</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">Apple or Google handle all payments. We never see your card or bank details.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Selling and ads</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">We do not sell or rent your information, show ads, or track you across other apps and websites.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. Information that stays on your phone -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">3. Information that stays on your phone</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The following is created by you while using PantryPal and is stored only on your device, in a database encrypted with a key held in your phone's secure storage (iOS Keychain or Android Keystore). It is not sent to us, and we have no way to access it:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
          <li>Pantry items: food names, quantities, units, where they are kept (fridge, freezer, pantry) and freshness estimates.</li>
          <li>Shopping list items and what you have marked as bought.</li>
          <li>Recipes created for you, recipes you save, serving sizes and cooking progress.</li>
          <li>Scan history: the date of each scan and the food names it found (never the photo).</li>
          <li>Your "rescue" log of food you used in time.</li>
          <li>Preferences: theme, diets, allergies, household size, kitchen name, alert settings, your answer to the AI scanning consent (with the policy version you agreed to), and whether analytics is on.</li>
          <li>Subscription status and free plan usage counters (for example, how many free scans you have used this month).</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
          This information is deleted when you uninstall the app. You can also clear your pantry at any time in <strong>Settings</strong>, and export your pantry, list and recipes as a JSON file with <strong>Settings &gt; Export your data</strong>. If your phone backs up app data to iCloud or Google, that backup is controlled by Apple or Google under their own terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. Information that leaves your phone, and why -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">4. Information that leaves your phone, and why</h2>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3">4.1 AI photo scanning (OpenAI)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          PantryPal asks for your permission before the first scan. If you agree, each photo you take or pick (of shelves, a fridge, a pantry or a shop receipt) is resized, sent securely over HTTPS to OpenAI, L.L.C. (United States), and analysed to list the food in it. Only the photo and the instructions for reading it are sent.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
          <li>PantryPal does not store the photo. It is kept in the phone's memory only until you finish reviewing the results, then discarded.</li>
          <li>Requests are made with OpenAI's storage option turned off. Under OpenAI's API data policy, API data is not used to train OpenAI's models, and may be kept by OpenAI for up to 30 days only to detect abuse before being deleted.</li>
          <li>Please avoid photographing people, documents or anything other than food. If a photo contains other things, they are sent as part of the photo.</li>
          <li>You can turn AI scanning off at any time in <strong>Settings &gt; Photo scanning with AI</strong> and add items by hand instead.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3 mt-6">4.2 Recipe ideas (OpenAI)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          When recipes are created (after you confirm a scan, or when you tap Get recipes or New ideas), PantryPal sends OpenAI: the names, amounts and freshness of the foods in your pantry (or only the foods you picked), your chosen diets, your allergies and your household size. This is needed so that recipes use what you have and avoid what you cannot eat. Your allergies and diets may reveal information about your health or beliefs; they are sent only to create recipes, with the same no-storage and no-training terms as above. Leave them empty if you prefer not to share them.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3 mt-6">4.3 Barcode lookup (Open Food Facts)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          When you scan a product barcode, only the barcode number is sent to Open Food Facts, a non-profit open food database based in France, to find the product name. Like any website, Open Food Facts receives your IP address with the request.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3 mt-6">4.4 Usage analytics (Google Firebase Analytics)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          To understand which parts of the app are used, PantryPal sends Google Firebase Analytics: the names of screens you open, and two events with counts only (how many items a scan added or updated, and how many recipes were created). Firebase also records a random app-instance identifier, the app version, device model, operating system, language and an approximate country derived from the IP address. PantryPal turns off advertising ID collection, Android ID collection and Apple's vendor identifier collection. We never send food names, anything you type, photos or your location.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Analytics is on when you first install the app. You can turn it off at any time in <strong>Settings &gt; Share usage analytics</strong>, and nothing about how you use the app is sent after that.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3 mt-6">4.5 Crash reports (Google Firebase Crashlytics)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          If the app crashes or hits an error, a crash report is sent to Google Firebase Crashlytics so we can fix it. It contains technical details such as the error, the code location, app version, device model, operating system, free memory and disk space, and a random installation identifier. Any extra context we add is limited to counts and error types, never your food names or anything you type. Crash reports are used only to find and fix bugs.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3 mt-6">4.6 App configuration (Google Firebase Remote Config)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          At launch, the app fetches its settings from Google Firebase Remote Config. This uses a random Firebase installation identifier and your IP address, and does not include any of your kitchen data.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3 mt-6">4.7 Subscriptions and payments (Apple and Google)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          Pro subscriptions are bought through the Apple App Store or Google Play. Apple or Google process the payment under their own privacy policies. PantryPal receives only what it needs to unlock Pro: which plan is active, whether it is a free trial, the renewal or expiry date, and a purchase token. We never receive your name, email, card or bank details. Purchase status is checked directly with Apple or Google on your phone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. Features that never send data -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">5. Features that never send data</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Voice commands in cook mode:</strong> speech is recognised by your phone's own on-device recogniser (PantryPal requires on-device mode). No audio is recorded, stored or sent anywhere.</li>
          <li><strong>Read-aloud:</strong> recipe steps are spoken by your phone's built-in text-to-speech.</li>
          <li><strong>Alerts:</strong> "Use today" and scan reminders are local notifications scheduled on your phone. We do not use push notifications and do not collect a push token.</li>
          <li><strong>Photo library:</strong> when you pick a photo to scan, the app can read only the photo you choose.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 6. Phone permissions -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">6. Phone permissions</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm sm:text-base border border-gray-200">
            <thead class="bg-gray-50">
              <tr>
                <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Permission</th>
                <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Why PantryPal asks</th>
                <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Required?</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Camera</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">To scan your fridge, pantry, receipts and barcodes.</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">Only for scanning</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Photos (picker)</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">To scan a photo you already took.</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">Optional</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Microphone and Speech Recognition</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">To hear "next", "back", "repeat" and "how long" in cook mode, on the phone only.</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">Optional, Pro</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Notifications</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">For "Use today" alerts, scan reminders and cook timers.</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">Optional</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
          You can change any permission in your phone's Settings at any time. The app works without them, except for the features that need them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 7. Why we use information (legal bases) -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">7. Why we use information (legal bases)</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Where the EU or UK General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) applies, we rely on:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Your consent</strong> for AI photo scanning, for sending your diets and allergies to create recipes, and for usage analytics. You can withdraw consent at any time in Settings; this does not affect processing done before.</li>
          <li><strong>Performance of a contract</strong> to provide the app and your Pro subscription, including recipe creation and barcode lookup.</li>
          <li><strong>Our legitimate interests</strong> in keeping the app working and secure, through crash reports and configuration, in a way that uses no content and random identifiers only.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
          Under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, we process personal data on the basis of your consent, given in the app, and for the legitimate uses that the Act allows.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 8. Who we share information with -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">8. Who we share information with</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          We share information only with the service providers named above, and only for the purposes described: OpenAI (AI scanning and recipes), Google (Firebase Analytics, Crashlytics and Remote Config), Open Food Facts (barcode lookup), and Apple and Google (app stores and payments). Each processes data under its own terms and privacy policy.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          We may also disclose information if required by law, to respond to a valid legal request, to protect the rights, safety or property of users or others, or as part of a sale or transfer of the app, in which case this policy continues to apply. We do not sell or "share" personal information for cross-context behavioural advertising, as those terms are defined under US state privacy laws.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 9. International transfers -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">9. International transfers</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          OpenAI and Google process data in the United States and other countries, which may have different data protection laws from your own. Where the GDPR applies, these transfers rely on the providers' Standard Contractual Clauses or the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, as applicable. Transfers from India are made in line with the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and any restrictions notified under it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 10. How long information is kept -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">10. How long information is kept</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm sm:text-base border border-gray-200">
            <thead class="bg-gray-50">
              <tr>
                <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Information</th>
                <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Kept for</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Kitchen data on your phone</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">Until you delete it in the app or uninstall the app.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Photos</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">Not stored by PantryPal. Kept in memory only until you finish reviewing a scan. OpenAI may keep API data for up to 30 days for abuse monitoring.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Recipe requests</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">Not stored by PantryPal outside your phone. Same OpenAI terms as photos.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Analytics data</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">Up to 14 months in Google Analytics, then deleted automatically.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Crash reports</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">Up to 90 days in Firebase Crashlytics.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 align-top">Emails you send us (including feedback from the app, which opens your email app)</th>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 align-top">As long as needed to answer you, and no longer than 2 years.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 11. Security -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">11. Security</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          Your kitchen data is stored in an encrypted database on your phone, with its key held in the phone's secure hardware-backed storage. All data sent off the phone travels over encrypted HTTPS connections. No method of storage or transmission is perfectly secure, but we take reasonable measures to protect information and will notify you and the authorities of a personal data breach where the law requires it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 12. Your rights and choices -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">12. Your rights and choices</h2>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3">Choices in the app</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
          <li>Turn AI photo scanning off or on: <strong>Settings &gt; Photo scanning with AI</strong>.</li>
          <li>Turn usage analytics off or on: <strong>Settings &gt; Share usage analytics</strong>.</li>
          <li>Change or remove your diets and allergies: <strong>Settings &gt; Taste profile</strong>.</li>
          <li>Export your data: <strong>Settings &gt; Export your data</strong>.</li>
          <li>Clear your pantry: <strong>Settings &gt; Clear pantry</strong>. Uninstalling the app deletes all of its data from the phone.</li>
          <li>Manage or cancel your subscription in your App Store or Google Play account, or from <strong>Settings &gt; Manage subscription</strong>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3 mt-6">Your legal rights</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete or receive a copy of your personal data, to object to or restrict processing, to withdraw consent, and to complain to a data protection authority. This includes:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>India (DPDP Act, 2023):</strong> the right to information about processing, correction and erasure, grievance redressal, and to nominate a person to exercise your rights in case of death or incapacity. If you are not satisfied with our response, you may complain to the Data Protection Board of India.</li>
          <li><strong>EU, EEA and UK (GDPR):</strong> the rights listed above, including data portability and the right to lodge a complaint with your local supervisory authority.</li>
          <li><strong>United States (including California):</strong> the right to know, access, correct and delete personal information, and not to be discriminated against for using these rights. We do not sell or share personal information for targeted advertising, so there is nothing to opt out of.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
          Because PantryPal has no accounts and keeps your kitchen data on your phone, most of it can be viewed, exported and deleted directly in the app. The data held by our providers (analytics and crash reports) is linked only to random identifiers, so we may need you to share the identifier shown in your request, or we may be unable to link it to you. To make a request, email <a href="mailto:contact@coachie-ai.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">contact@coachie-ai.com</a>. We will reply within 30 days, or sooner where the law requires.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 13. Children -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">13. Children</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          PantryPal is not directed to children under 13, and you must be at least 13 to use it. If you are under 18 (or the age of majority where you live), you may use PantryPal only with the permission and supervision of a parent or guardian, who should agree to this policy and to any purchase. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 13. If you believe a child has used AI scanning or sent us information, contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@coachie-ai.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">contact@coachie-ai.com</a> and we will help remove it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 14. Changes to this policy -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">14. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          We may update this policy as the app changes. We will post the new version at this address with a new "Last updated" date. If a change affects what is sent to our AI partner, PantryPal will ask for your consent again inside the app before your next scan.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 15. Contact -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">15. Contact</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Veera</p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-2">
          <strong>Email:</strong>{' '}
          <a href="mailto:contact@coachie-ai.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">
            contact@coachie-ai.com
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</MainLayout>
